  entry
    definition "an explanation of something that is not immediately obvious"
    examples ("the edict was subject to many interpretations" "he annoyed us with his interpreting of parables" "often imitations are extended to provide a more accurate rendition of the child's intended meaning")
    id oewn-05774244-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (interpretation interpreting rendition)
  entry
    definition "the act of interpreting something as expressed in an artistic performance"
    examples ("her rendition of Milton's verse was extraordinarily moving")
    id oewn-00101363-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (rendition interpretation)
  entry
    definition "a written communication in a second language having the same meaning as the written communication in a first language"
    id oewn-06548380-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (translation "interlingual rendition" version)
